  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life-Saving IDP and Famine Response in Blue Nile State: Addressing Urgent Needs in Damazine and Roseries.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtRI and its partner,&#xa0;Al Salam Organization for Rehabilitation and Development (AORD), aim to improve access to quality, gender-sensitive primary healthcare services for vulnerable internally displaced persons (IDPs) and host communities in Damazine and Roseries localities, Blue Nile State. Through a multidisciplinary approach, the project will directly implement health and nutrition activities and integrate WASH and protection services&#xa0;at MMU and community levels. This includes providing mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) and establishing four mobile clinics to reach&#xa0;32,000 individuals benefiting from health services through 4 Medical Mobile Units (MMUs) and 22,815 benefiting from nutrition services.ltbrgt ltbrgtIn addition to healthcare services, RI will address acute malnutrition by implementing Community-Based Management of Acute Malnutrition (CMAM) services, including Outpatient Therapeutic Programs (OTP) in targeted areas. The project will offer life-saving treatment for Severe Acute Malnutrition (SAM) and Moderate Acute Malnutrition (MAM), while also focusing on preventative measures by engaging mothers, pregnant and lactating women (PLW), and men in promoting healthier family care practices.ltbrgt ltbrgtWASH and protection activities will be fully integrated into the health interventions to ensure comprehensive support and a holistic response to the needs of the affected populations.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
